// The Wise Old Man, Draynor Village.
//
// REPORTED FROM THE GAME as "there are two wise old men in draynor", and there were. He was already
// on the map and had been all along - not as [wise_old_man] but as [wom_multi], the multinpc at
// 3088,3255 inside his own house, which resolves to wise_old_man at every Swan Song step it lists
// and is who skillcape_shop.rs2 sells the Quest point cape through. A search for the npc by name
// missed him, so a second one was spawned at 3088,3251 outside, four tiles from the first, and both
// stood there with the same name and the same Talk-to. That spawn is gone from maps/m48_50.jm2 and
// everything hangs off the one who was always there.
//
// Which also means the trigger name matters: Player.getOpTrigger reads NpcType.get(target.type) -
// the shell standing in the world - so an [opnpc1] on the resolved child never fires. It has to be
// wom_multi, which is why the cape dialogue was written on wom_multi in the first place.
//
// WHEN HE IS NOT HERE. wom_multi lists swansong 0, 5, 10, 15, 20, 190 and 200 and nothing between,
// so from the moment he leaves for Piscatoris (^swan_wom = 30) until he is back and told about it
// (^swan_told = 190) there is no Wise Old Man in Draynor at all. That is the quest's own doing and
// it is right: he is at the fishing colony. It does mean Garden of Tranquillity cannot reach him
// mid-Swan-Song, which was true before this too.
//
// The two quest hooks go first and each one answers only at the step that wants him, which is the
// rule the Rat Catchers hook on Gertrude broke: a ~x_wants that keys on "my quest has not started"
// takes the npc away from everybody for ever. Garden of Tranquillity needs him to enchant the Ring
// of Charos; Swan Song needs him because Herman Caranos writes to "a man in Draynor who is supposed
// to be the best magician alive and who has spent thirty years pretending to be a pensioner".

[opnpc1,wom_multi]
if (~garden_wom_wants = true) {
    @garden_wom;
}
if (~swan_wom_wants = true) {
    @swan_wom_draynor_talk;
}
// His own conversation, which is the Quest point cape - it predates both quests and lives with the
// other skillcape masters.
@wom_cape_talk;
